\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A marked sign edge on the two-by-two torus}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{Choose a positive horizontal edge #{e_0} of the labeled
sign torus in \ref{fdip-010H}. Its [scalar path pairing](fdip-011B)
is #{\check U_{e_0}}, the reduced link of \ref{fdip-010Z}. To sum the
joint weight times this observable, select a face subset #{A} and
a hopping-edge subset #{B} in the expansion of its #{12} factors
#{(3+z)/2}. Let #{E_A} be the odd boundary of #{A}. The extra
marked link sign forces #{B=E_A\mathbin{\triangle}\{e_0\}},
the symmetric difference. Every other selection has a link sign
of odd exponent and sums to zero. The edge set contributing site
signs with odd multiplicity is then
#{B\mathbin{\triangle}\{e_0\}=E_A}. Each selected face has even
incidence at every vertex, so all site exponents are even.
Summing the monomial over all
#{2^{12}} configurations cancels its denominator #{2^{12}}.}

\p{Of the #{4} singleton face sets, two have #{e_0} on their
boundary, as do their complements. The #{4} neighboring pairs
have boundary size #{4}. The two faces incident
to the horizontal marked edge lie in the same column. Each row
pair therefore contains exactly one of them, whereas a column
pair contains both or neither. Both diagonal pairs
separate them and have boundary size #{8}. The empty and full
face sets have empty boundary. Toggling #{e_0} decreases each
boundary size by one if it contains the edge and increases it by
one otherwise. Thus summing #{3^{12-|A|-|B|}} gives the numerator
##{\begin{aligned}
 &3^{11}+2(3^8+3^6)+2(3^7+3^5)\\
 &\qquad+2\cdot3^3+2(3^6+3^4)+3^7
 =200448.
\end{aligned}}}

\p{In the reduced sum of \ref{fdip-0110} the observable is just
#{V_{e_0}}. The same expansion forces the same subset #{B}, now
with only #{2^8} independent configurations in the sign sum.
Its numerator is #{200448/16=12528}. Both weighted means are
##{\frac{200448}{550656}=\frac{12528}{34416}=\frac{87}{239}.}}
